---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How I Check Evidence"
  description="How Shiwakshi Rashmi evaluates sources, distinguishes evidence from interpretation, and labels research confidence."
>
  <main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-12 md:py-16">
    <!-- Header -->
    <header class="space-y-4 mb-8">
      <p class="font-sans text-xs text-fg-muted uppercase tracking-wider">
        Evidence & checking policy
      </p>

      <h1 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-[2.6rem] font-normal text-fg leading-[1.15] tracking-tight">
        How I Check Evidence
      </h1>

      <p class="lede">
        This publication documents independent UX and market research inquiries. To ensure clarity and intellectual integrity, I apply specific checks before publishing any article.
      </p>
    </header>

    <hr class="border-t border-rule-strong my-8" />

    <!-- Evidence Status Guide as a One-Column <dl> at 16px per §4 -->
    <section class="space-y-6 mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-normal text-fg">
        Article status classifications
      </h2>
      <p class="summary">
        Every article on this website carries a research status indicating its evidentiary scope:
      </p>

      <dl class="space-y-6 pt-2 font-sans text-base max-w-[38rem]">
        <!-- Literature Exploration -->
        <div class="space-y-1 py-3 border-b border-rule">
          <dt class="font-serif text-lg font-normal text-fg">
            Literature exploration
          </dt>
          <dd class="text-fg-body text-base leading-relaxed m-0 pt-1">
            Surveys published secondary research, peer-reviewed papers, and sociological frameworks to map what is already established about a human question.
          </dd>
        </div>

        <!-- Research in Progress -->
        <div class="space-y-1 py-3 border-b border-rule">
          <dt class="font-serif text-lg font-normal text-fg">
            Research in progress
          </dt>
          <dd class="text-fg-body text-base leading-relaxed m-0 pt-1">
            Documents active investigations, qualitative fieldwork frameworks, or conceptual interaction models that are undergoing iterative reflection.
          </dd>
        </div>

        <!-- Critical Review -->
        <div class="space-y-1 py-3 border-b border-rule">
          <dt class="font-serif text-lg font-normal text-fg">
            Critical review
          </dt>
          <dd class="text-fg-body text-base leading-relaxed m-0 pt-1">
            Evaluates existing tools, software paradigms, or research methodologies against empirical evidence, identifying where current conventions fall short.
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <!-- The 4 Checks -->
    <section class="prose max-w-[38rem] pt-6 border-t border-rule space-y-6">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-normal text-fg">
        The checks I conduct before publishing
      </h2>
      <p>
        I apply four checks to my writing:
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li>
          <strong>Primary Source Verification:</strong> Citations are traced to their original published source, verified DOI link, or archival publication. I do not cite secondary summaries without examining the source material.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Explicit Separation of Claims:</strong> I strictly separate what empirical literature demonstrates from my own interpretive reflections as a UX practitioner. Where evidence is inconclusive, I explicitly label it.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Methodological Boundary Declaration:</strong> I state the limitations of every qualitative observation, sample size, or framework. Small qualitative cohorts are not generalised to population-wide conclusions.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Non-Clinical Scope Discipline:</strong> In writing on chronic and fluctuating conditions, I evaluate user experience, interface burden, and human behaviour outside clinic walls. I never make medical, diagnostic, or clinical claims.
        </li>
      </ol>

      <!-- Dated Correction Policy (§4) -->
      <div class="mt-8 pt-6 border-t border-rule font-sans text-xs text-fg-muted space-y-2">
        <strong class="text-fg block uppercase tracking-wider">Correction policy</strong>
        <p class="m-0 leading-relaxed">
          When a citation, claim, or data point is found to be in error, I correct it directly in the text and append a dated correction note at the foot of the inquiry.
        </p>
        <p class="m-0 text-fg-muted">
          Last updated: 4 November 2026.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-6 pt-4 border-t border-rule font-sans text-xs text-fg-muted">
        <strong class="text-fg block mb-1">Independent publication note</strong>
        <span>Articles on this website are written and edited independently. They reflect my professional practice, literature synthesis, and design reflections. They are not academic peer-reviewed journal papers or clinical trial reports.</span>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
